[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777236061","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104987#issuecomment-2777236061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104987","id":2777236061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6liUJd","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T23:57:14Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T23:57:14Z","body":"cc @syntaxerror247 \n\nThe script in question can be found on this page: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/2d/2d_movement.html#way-movement","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777236061/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777501716","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104987#issuecomment-2777501716","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104987","id":2777501716,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ljVAU","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T04:00:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T04:00:19Z","body":"I can also reproduce this with `Gboard` and for me it happens whenever I copy and paste code using the virtual keyboard. I thought there was already an issue reported for this, but I couldn’t find it at the moment.\n\nThe core issue is that when you copy code, it includes the original indentation and when pasting using a virtual keyboard (Gboard in my case), the paste is processed through our input handling mechanism, which internally uses an `EditText` widget. This results in each character being inserted one by one. So if a line starts with indentation, that indentation is preserved but then the `Script Editor` also applies its own indentation logic.\n\nTo clarify, here’s an example.\n\nOriginal copied code:\n```\nextends Control\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tDisplayServer.set_hardware_keyboard_status_change_callback(callback)\n```\n\nAfter pasting into the Script Editor using the virtual keyboard:\n```\nextends Control\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tDisplayServer.set_hardware_keyboard_status_change_callback(callback)\n```\n\nAs you can see, the `extends` and `func` lines are fine because they had no initial indentation. But inside the `_ready` function, the line has two tabs instead of one. This happens because the original indentation is pasted, and then the Script Editor adds another tab due to its auto-indent behavior for new code blocks.\n\nSo ultimately, this seems to be an issue with how input from virtual keyboards is handled during paste operations. Fixing this might require considerable amount of work as we would have to most probably change our virtual keyboard input handling mechanism.\n\nAs a workaround: You can paste code snippets using the `context menu` or the `Edit menu` at the top. This method works correctly and avoids the extra indentation issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777501716/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777513167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104987#issuecomment-2777513167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104987","id":2777513167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ljXzP","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}"